+## 10. mmproj verdict — confirmed on :8089 (spec-replay)
+
+Both spec arms ran with `--mmproj .../Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-mmproj-Q8_0.gguf
+--no-mmproj-offload` (A-greedy/notes.txt, B-greedy/notes.txt cmd lines), no
+exit, no "not supported by this context"/"unsupported batch.has_embd" log
+lines, and drafts were actually drafted: A draft_n=11565/accepted=6609, B
+5535/2160 (summed over 84 fg rows). The §3 static verdict is confirmed on the
+live server: ngram speculation works with `--mmproj` loaded for text-only
+traffic. The `unsupported batch.has_embd + spec case` throw (server-context.cpp:
+3550-3553) fires only when a batch carries embeddings (image input); the replay
+is text-only and image + spec remains untested. No "restore checkpoint" lines
+in any A/B phase, i.e., checkpoint-mode speculation was not needed.
+
+## 11. off/prod rerun (r6) — corrected probe, verified
+
+Re-run after the t0-before-bg-start and t_end-per-row fixes; exit 0, 883 s
+(results/2026-10-12/autopilot/spec-replay-r6.log). Verified:
+
+- all 4 phases carry `[phase] window t0=... t_fg_end=... t_join_end=...` lines
+  in off-prod/notes.txt; 140/140 rows carry t_end.
+- fg tok/s: single-agent 56.0, single-mem 55.6, dual-agent 31.3, dual-mem 25.4.
+- combined two-slot throughput (fg + bg rows ending before fg, / fg wall s):
+  single-agent 43.8, single-mem 32.7, dual-agent 47.8, dual-mem 35.4.
+  This is a conservative completed-output measure, not exact aggregate decode
+  tok/s: a bg request still in flight at fg end is excluded (spec_analyze.py).
+- spec off; prod sampling, so out_sha256 is not comparable across arms.
+
+## 12. State and decision so far
+
+Greedy (all 4 phases present per arm; A/B carry draft_n/draft_n_accepted on all
+84 fg rows; off has no draft fields by design, noted in notes.txt):
+
+| phase | off | A | B |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| single-agent fg tok/s | 55.1 | 86.0 (54.3 no-length) | 53.4 |
+| single-mem fg tok/s | 55.6 | 53.1 | 50.7 |
+| dual-agent fg tok/s | 26.3 | 25.5 (26.1 no-length) | 23.0 |
+| dual-mem fg tok/s | 25.0 | 23.8 | 22.4 |
+
+No arm beats off with both slots busy (dual-agent 26.3 / 25.5 / 23.0;
+dual-mem 25.0 / 23.8 / 22.4). Per the plan rule, the remaining prod run is A
+(highest dual-agent greedy fg of A/B: 25.5 vs 23.0).
+
+Outstanding: A-prod run (turnstile lease, :8089). If its combined dual
+throughput does not beat off-prod 47.8 tok/s (and no other metric reverses the
+picture), the decision is **no-deploy**: speculation does not help real agent
+traffic with both slots busy. A no-deploy note must then state that (a) `--spec-
+type ngram-mod` changes temperature-0 outputs even with draft_n 0 (baseline-r0/
+0/0: off 530c... vs A cdad... vs B f20f...) and (b) image input with spec on
+is untested (has_embd throw).
